wall
====
not quite bleeding-edge wlroots, wayland (server), and xkb bindings for go; part of the concorde cross-protocol window system: by supporting the wayland backend.

ACHTUNG! these bindings are NOT general-purpose (yet) hence there is no guarantee that they will be sufficient for your use case.

compiling:
----------
install a `wlroots` version between 0.20.0 and 0.21 (exclusive), `wayland`, `libxkbcommon`, and `pkg-config` via your preferred package manager.

on arch, wlroots is split into different packages per minor release number; install `wlroots0.20`.
on void, install `wlroots-devel`, `wayland-devel`, and `libxkbcommon-devel`.
on gentoo/exherbo, at least ensure that the `x11-backend` USE flag is set for `wlroots` and set the `wayland`, `X`, and `xwayland` USE flags globally or for all relevant packages.

there is a tinywl implementation in `cmd/tinywl` that can be built with `go build`.

prior art:
----------
https://github.com/DeedleFake/wlr
https://github.com/swaywm/go-wlroots
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wlroots/wlroots/-/blob/0.20/tinywl/tinywl.c
